  "question": {
    "text": "A point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> moves such that the chord of contact of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> with respect to the circle <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> passes through the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> The coordinates of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> when it is nearest to the origin are",
