  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let, the point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> be <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> then<br />Equation of the chord of contact is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;<br />Since, it passes through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> so,<br />&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> is the locus of the point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />Hence, the nearest point on <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>",
    "image": null
